  "definition": "Recall is a classification metric that measures the fraction of actual positive cases that a model correctly identifies. It matters when missing a positive case is more costly than producing a false alarm.",
  "intuition": "Count how many real positives you captured, not just how many predictions were correct overall.",
  "mathematical_foundation": "$$\n\\text{Recall} = \\frac{TP}{TP + FN}\n$$\n\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `TP` | True positives |\n| `FN` | False negatives |",
